title Mycelium Chorus r2 — the whole quorum travels, and the quorum law survives the wire
prompt baton prin recur — read REMEMBER + the 1,024-round itinerary + the six-season double-seat, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, approve own design rounds, send each finished increment as its own signed round, stop at custody gates.
think r1 gathered a Chorus (a bounded quorum of independent Vouchers for one account position at one order-head) and proved verify_chorus(threshold) is believed only when a threshold of distinct nodes agree. A quorum a holder cannot hand to another is only local, so r2 lets the whole Chorus cross as bytes (mirroring voucher_bron / statement_bron).
think Design seam: because every member attests the SAME claim, the wire names the claim once — head · account · position · threshold — then one `member <node-hex> <sig-hex>` line per voice. Each member carries only its own node key and signature; the head/account/position it signed are the shared claim. This is compact and structurally honest — a member reconstructed on parse cannot disagree on position (it is rebuilt from the claim), so the disagreement failure is an in-memory-gather property, while the wire's live refusals are BadSignature (a forged member), DuplicateNode (a padded record), BelowThreshold (a thin record), and the malformed-field family.
think Implemented mycelium/chorus_bron.rye: render(c, threshold, out) writes the claim lines then a member line per voice; parse(text, out) reconstructs each Voucher from the claim + the member's node/sig, appends via chorus.add_voucher, then — the crux — re-runs chorus.verify_chorus(out, threshold) at the record's own stated threshold, mapping its ChorusError into BronError, so a record that does not prove its own quorum refuses before trust. Reused voucher_bron's hex/token helpers; two contract asserts per function; parse_int for the u64 positions and the u32 threshold (threshold < 1 refuses BadInt).
obs First build failed honestly and was fixed in one pass: the ChorusError set is declared (not inferred), so it includes TooManyMembers even though verify_chorus never returns it — Zig required the catch-switch to be exhaustive; added an explicit `error.TooManyMembers => return error.TooManyMembers` branch (kept exhaustive; verify never gathers). Then GREEN: a three-voice open-pledge chorus renders to a format chorus-v1 record and parses back byte-for-byte (fixed point), the recovered quorum proves itself at threshold 2 offline and checks against the ledger it vouches; the threshold survives the crossing (thr == 2).
obs The quorum-law refusals all hold on the wire: a forged member (one signature byte flipped, rendered then parsed) → BadSignature; a record rendered at threshold 4 with three voices → BelowThreshold; a record padded with node[0] twice → DuplicateNode; and a bad header · unknown field · missing threshold line · bad hex node key each refuse. Composes chorus + voucher public API only, editing none (the Chorus r1 re-runs GREEN at the door). Witness tools/mycelium_chorus_bron_witness.rish GREEN, TAME bans clean, width-check exit 0. Demo seeds — no key/funds/network/custody.
loom witness=mycelium_chorus_bron_witness max_record=8192 refusals=7 first_build=switch_exhaustive_fix first_run=green
file mycelium/chorus_bron.rye r2 — the format chorus-v1 record (claim named once, one member line per voice), render · parse (reconstruct + re-verify the quorum at the stated threshold)
file tools/mycelium_chorus_bron_witness.rish the r2 witness — fixed-point + quorum-survives-wire + refusal assertions, the Chorus r1 re-run at the door
recommend keep-going Chorus r3 (the quorum reads across a Knot — a chorus gathered over a ledger resolved across an epoch cut, the vouched position continuous across the join and every member's order-head folding the whole agreed order, base included), then r4 true to the bytes (a real on-disk Cord fixture, app == awk, the distinct-node count and each recomputed order-head matching). A served chorus · per-account mint authority · breach renames (cairn-first) · deep debride · seed force-push stay the maintainer's hand.
